DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       sseemm__ddeessttrrooyy()  destroys the unnamed semaphore at the address pointed to
       by _s_e_m.

       Only a semaphore that has been initialized by sseemm__iinniitt(3) should be de‐
       stroyed using sseemm__ddeessttrrooyy().

       Destroying a semaphore that other processes or  threads  are  currently
       blocked on (in sseemm__wwaaiitt(3)) produces undefined behavior.

       Using  a  semaphore that has been destroyed produces undefined results,
       until the semaphore has been reinitialized using sseemm__iinniitt(3).

